    "description": "Keep, level 1 of 3: shell and fittings (what soldiers build first). A grand stone keep after the approved sample: 15 x 15 on a cobblestone apron, four corner towers with corbelled tops, a gatehouse with an arched passage, battlements on corbels, a great hall with a throne, tables and a hearth, stairs (no ladders) to the king's rooms and the roof deck. 16 tall: needs scaffold in game.",
    "changes": "Dark oak ties it to the kingdom look: a dark oak door frame (level 1) and low dark oak pyramid roofs that close the four tower tops (level 1, no more open boxes); level 3 now has its own feature, timber hoardings (dark oak posts and pent roofs) over every battlement.",
